Let's pick a different name for this, to avoid the _death_ connection. Perhaps a tiny atomic lock like [this one](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/atomic/#examples)?

```rust
use std::sync::Arc;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};
use std::thread;

fn main() {
    // Say we have a spinlock, which can be acquired so long as its value is `0`
    // In this example, the lock is already acquired
    let spinlock = Arc::new(AtomicUsize::new(1));

    // Spawn off a thread that will release the lock at some point
    let spinlock_clone = spinlock.clone();
    let thread = thread::spawn(move|| {
        // Do some work, knowing we have the lock
        spinlock_clone.store(0, Ordering::SeqCst);
    });

    // Wait for the other thread to release the lock
    // We do this in a loop, using `hint::spin_loop` to signal that we're waiting
    while spinlock.load(Ordering::SeqCst) != 0 {
        // Signal to the processor that we're in a busy-wait loop
        hint::spin_loop();
    }
}
```

