I suggest to keep the rules syntactic and do not look at resolutions, like in all other cases of destructuring.

The `DefKind::Ctor(..)` check is both too relaxed (the correct condition is `DefKind::Ctor(_, CtorKind::Fn)`), and, what is worse, too restrictive, because this check will reject cases like these
```rust
Self(a, b) = ...;

enum E { V(u8, u16) }
type A = E;
A::V(a, b) = ...;
```
for which we don't know the resolution during AST lowering, and determine it only during type checking.

