The path to the impl is actually independent of the path to the self type, as in this [example](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2018&gist=2d8bddc90fea0703e8e5d829302711ae):

```rust

pub mod foo {
    pub struct X;
}

mod bar {
    impl super::foo::X {
        pub fn bar() {}
    } 
}
```

So the version that does not print the path to the impl is actually the correct one. The symbol mangling RFC has [a section](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/2603-rust-symbol-name-mangling-v0.html#methods) describing the situation in a bit more detail.

