This moves from the heap to the heap. Suggestion: "and moves `t`into it"

If you look at MIR, you can see that dereferencing actually moves it to the stack and then calls `Arc::from`. It might look like it is moving from the heap to the heap, but you have to call it with ownership, and it is on the stack.

